{#- The turn intent block (roadmap 02 §6.5): what a play decision chose for
    the assigned actor's next contribution, sent as its own system message
    after the history -- placed as an author's note at depth 0 is, and never
    a catalog section, so a prompt layout cannot switch it off while its call
    is still paid, and it breaks no cached prefix before it.
    Vars: name (the actor's name); stance, disclosure, tension: the
    descriptions of the answers that were read (`turn_plan/stance.j2`,
    `turn_plan/disclosure.j2`, `turn_plan/tension.j2`), each "" when that
    question was not asked or not answered. At least one is non-empty, or
    nothing is sent. -#}
{%- if stance -%}
{{ name }}'s approach in this reply: {{ stance }}.
{% endif -%}
{%- if disclosure -%}
Of what {{ name }} already knows, they {{ disclosure }}.
{% endif -%}
{%- if tension -%}
In this reply, {{ tension }}.
{% endif -%}
Write it in their own voice. Never name or explain the approach.
